	// statement is signed ES256, and one whose header names any other `alg` is not verified. A
	// Mac's Secure Enclave and a TPM both make such a key, and it never leaves them.
	//
	// A CERTIFICATE IS VALID FOR 90 DAYS, AND IT IS RENEWED HERE. Every token answers when the
	// certificate that signed its statement stops being valid. When 30 days or fewer are left,
	// the device makes a NEW key pair and sends a certificate request for it beside its next
