	//
	// AN INVITED GUEST SIGNS UP THE SAME WAY. An invitation is accepted afterwards, from the
	// person's own Companies → Requests, by somebody who holds the invited address confirmed
	// (Account's rule, ONPLO-1694). A sign-up carries no invitation, so a forwarded mail lets nobody
	// in.
	//
	// SHORT-LIVED AND SINGLE USE, as a sign-in is. Nothing is recorded anywhere until the sign-up
	// finishes: a person who walks away leaves no account behind.
