	// THE RECOVERY CODES ARE SHOWN ONCE, HERE, AND NEVER AGAIN. They are the only way back for a
	// person who loses every passkey (Account → Sign up, step 3). Onplo keeps none of them in the
	// clear, so nobody can show them a second time. They are not yet counted as a way in: the
	// person says they kept them, on Settings → Security (decision 0614).
	//
	// THE SESSION LANDS IN THE PERSONAL ENVIRONMENT, the only one the person has (step 5). Its
	// `proved_at` is the moment of this passkey touch.
	//
	// ONE ANSWER PER SIGN-UP. Completed, refused or expired, a sign-up is spent, and its id answers
