// certificate that signed its statement stops being valid. When 30 days or fewer are left,
// the device makes a NEW key pair and sends a certificate request for it beside its next
// statement; the answer carries the new certificate as well as the token. The old certificate
// stays in force until the first statement the new key signs is traded, and ends then. A
// device that lost that answer sends the same request again and is answered the same
// certificate. A device whose certificate ran out can no longer prove itself here: it is
// enrolled again.
