// RequestTokensWithBody Trade an app's one-time code for the person's session, or renew that session
//
// THE TOKEN ENDPOINT (RFC 6749 §4.1.3 and §6, OpenID Connect Core §3.1.3; architecture decision
// record 037). An app that `grantAuthorizationCode` sent back with a code trades it here, once
// (`grant_type=authorization_code`), for:
//
//   - THE ACCESS TOKEN, which is the person's session, opaque, read by every Onplo service as every
//     session is. It records the app it was issued to.
//   - THE REFRESH TOKEN, opaque, which renews that session before it ends.
//   - THE ID TOKEN, a JWT signed with a key of `readProviderKeySet`, which says who signed in: `iss`,
//     `sub` (the person), `aud` (the app), `exp`, `iat`, `auth_time`, `amr` and the `nonce` the app
//     sent. It is for the app alone and NO ONPLO SERVICE TAKES IT AS A BEARER.
//
// THE CODE IS TRADED ONLY BY THE APP IT WAS HANDED TO: the same `client_id`, the same
// `redirect_uri`, and a `code_verifier` whose SHA-256 is the challenge it was asked with (RFC 7636).
// A CODE SHOWN A SECOND TIME IS REFUSED, AND THE SESSION ITS FIRST TRADE OPENED IS ENDED, because a
// code shown twice is a code somebody else holds.
//
// RENEWED WITH THE REFRESH TOKEN (`grant_type=refresh_token`, record 037 rule Four): the same app
// hands it back, with `client_id`, and is answered a new session, a new refresh token and a new ID
// token. Each refresh token is good ONCE. ONE SHOWN AFTER IT WAS SPENT ENDS ITS WHOLE FAMILY,
// every refresh token since the code and every session they came with (OAuth 2.1 §4.3.1). A
// renewed session is as fresh as the passkey touch, never as the renewal, and the family lives
// thirty days from that touch, renewed or not. A suspended member's tokens end with the
// suspension.
//
// REFUSED AS OAUTH REFUSES (RFC 6749 §5.2), with a 400 and an `error`, so any OAuth client reads
// it: a field missing is `invalid_request`, a grant other than these two is
// `unsupported_grant_type`, a code or refresh token unknown, expired, spent, revoked or shown by
// another app is `invalid_grant`, told apart from nothing, and a renewal asking a scope it was
// never granted is `invalid_scope`.
//
// SIGNED OUT, because the code is the proof, and LIMITED by how often it is called (decision 0732).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /token (the `RequestTokens` operationId).
