// ReadProviderKeySetWithResponse Read the public keys that check the provider's tokens
//
// THE KEY SET (RFC 7517): the public half of every key whose ID tokens may still be in a client's
// hands. A client checks an ID token's signature with the key its header names by `kid`.
//
// THE PRIVATE HALF NEVER LEAVES ONPLO'S KEY SERVICE: identity asks it to sign, and reads only the
// public half to publish here.
//
// ACROSS A ROTATION THERE ARE TWO: the key signing now, and the one before it, kept for at least a
// day after the change, so a token signed just before it is still checked. A `kid` is the key's own
// thumbprint (RFC 7638), so one id never names two keys.
//
// SIGNED OUT AND LIMITED, as the discovery document is. It may be kept for five minutes; a client
// that meets a `kid` it does not know reads it again.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
