// AuthorizeSignInWithResponse Send a person from an app to sign in
//
// THE AUTHORIZATION ENDPOINT (OpenID Connect Core §3.1.2, architecture decision record 037). An
// app sends the browser here with its request, and Onplo answers one of three ways:
//
//   - BACK TO THE APP WITH ITS CODE, at once, when the browser keeps a live sign-in
//     (`keepSignInForBrowser`, record 037 rule Five) and the person still belongs where it
//     landed. No second passkey touch. The code lands where the kept sign-in landed.
//   - TO THE SIGN-IN SCREEN, carrying the request, when the app, its return address and every
//     field are ones Onplo takes and no sign-in is kept. The screen asks for the passkey, then
//     `grantAuthorizationCode` and `keepSignInForBrowser` send the browser back to the app with
//     its code.
