//     lists. A code or an error sent to an address nobody registered is how a sign-in is stolen.
//
// THE FIELDS ARE READ BY THE RULES OF `AuthorizationRequest`, not by the parameters' own bounds:
// each is optional here so that a wrong one is answered as OAuth answers it, never as a 422.
//
